20:T5d2,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the UUID Generator free on ContentVerse India?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. All India utility tools on ContentVerse India are free to use with no sign-up required."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this an official government website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. ContentVerse India is an independent platform. We use public datasets and open APIs. For official records, use government portals like Parivahan, GST, FoSCoS, or ECI."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are these UUIDs truly unique?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Version 4 UUIDs are random with 122 bits of randomness, so the chance of a duplicate is negligible for any practical use."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are the UUIDs generated on a server?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. They are generated in your browser and are not sent or stored by ContentVerse India."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a UUID safe to use as a password or secret token?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A random v4 UUID is hard to guess, but for authentication use a purpose-built secret generator or a library designed for tokens."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between UUID and GUID?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"They are the same concept. GUID is the term used mostly in Microsoft ecosystems, while UUID is the standard name."}}]}16:[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"UUID Generator\",\"description\":\"Generate random UUID v4 identifiers for apps, databases, and APIs. Copy one or many at once.\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/uuid-generator\",\"applicationCategory\":\"UtilitiesApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Web\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"0\",\"priceCurrency\":\"